# vigil — Project Context

vigil is a monorepo of independent bootstrap sub-projects. Each sub-project has its own stack, conventions, and rule set.

## Sub-projects

| Project | Type | Description |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `api.vigil/` | Laravel 13 API (PHP 8.4) | Backend API bootstrap |
| `app.vigil/` | Vue 3 SPA (TypeScript) | Frontend web app bootstrap |
| `codelumen/` | VitePress | Code conventions documentation |
| `vitrum/` | Astro | Public/marketing website bootstrap |
| `liquen/` | Design tokens | Figma integration and design token management |
| `cortex/` | AI tooling | Source of truth for all AI rules and prompts |

## Rule routing

Rules are scoped to sub-projects via glob patterns. They activate automatically when you open or edit a matching file:

- Files in `api.vigil/**` → api.vigil architecture rules load
- Files in `app.vigil/**/*.vue` or `app.vigil/**/*.ts` → all 5 app.vigil Vue/TS rules load
- Any file → `shared-conventions` (always loaded) and this file (always loaded)

## Rule activation for planning sessions

Glob-scoped rules only activate when a matching file is open. During planning (no files open yet), load the relevant rules manually based on the projects involved.

When the user says they are working on **api.vigil**, read:

- `.cursor/rules/arcus-api-architecture.mdc`

When the user says they are working on **app.vigil**, read:

- `.cursor/rules/celer-01-vue-checklist.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/celer-02-vue-imports.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/celer-03-vue-script.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/celer-04-vue-template.mdc`
- `.cursor/rules/celer-05-module-conventions.mdc`

When working on **both**, read all of the above.

Do this at the start of every session before planning begins.

## AI tooling

- `cortex/` is the source of truth for all rules — never edit rules directly in sub-project folders; update cortex first, then sync
- Use `/sync-cortex` command to propagate cortex changes to all targets
- Use `cortex/start-session.md` for the planning session prompt template
